-- title:
--   Newform eigenplane in the Tate module of J₀(M), with Steinberg lines
-- statement:
--   Let $M \geq 1$, let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the project's sense (a normalised eigenform whose eigensystem occurs at no proper divisor of the level), let $\lambda$ be a prime and $S$ a finite set of naturals with $\lambda \in S$ and containing every prime divisor of $M$. Let $O'$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring, complete for its maximal-adic topology and with finite residue field, in which $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal, let $\chi_g \colon \mathbb{T} \to \mathbb{C}$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms generated by the Hecke operators away from $S$) with $\chi_g(T_\ell)$ equal to the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$ for every prime $\ell \nmid M$ outside $S$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the image of $\chi_g$ to $O'$. Then there is a ring $O''$ of the same type (a complete characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring with finite residue field), carrying an $O'$-algebra structure making it a finite $O'$-module with local and injective structure map, together with a $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-algebra structure, such that the following holds for every fraction field $K$ of $O''$. Equip $J_0(M) =$ `JZero M` (the degree-zero Picard group of the modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) with the Hecke-module structure `heckeModuleBar M`, and let $T =$ [`TateModule lam (JZero M)`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15), the Hecke-submodule of sequences $x \colon \mathbb{N} \to J_0(M)$ with $x_0 = 0$ and $\lambda \cdot x_{n+1} = x_n$. Then for any $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-module structure on $T$ acting on the $n$-th term through the reduction $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda \to \mathbb{Z}/\lambda^n$, any monoid homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ (the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$) to $\operatorname{End}_{O''}(O'' \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda} T)$ which on pure tensors is induced by the Galois action on sequences, and any ring homomorphism $T_M$ from [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlg`](def/HeckeGalois_EichlerShimura.html#L14) $= \mathrm{MvPolynomial}\ \mathrm{Nat.Primes}\ \mathbb{Z}$ to the same endomorphism ring which on pure tensors is induced by the Hecke action on $T$, there exists a $K$-submodule $W$ of $K \otimes_{O''} (O'' \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda} T)$ with $\dim_K W = 2$, stable under the base change of $\rho_M(\sigma)$ for every $\sigma$, such that: (i) for every prime $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$, the base change of $T_M(\mathrm{heckeGen}\ \ell)$ acts on $W$ as the scalar image in $K$ of $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))$; (ii) for such $\ell$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ acting as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, the trace on $W$ of the restriction of $\rho_M(\sigma)$ equals that same scalar; and (iii) for every prime $q \neq \lambda$ with $q \mid M$ and $q^2 \nmid M$ and every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, there are a one-dimensional $K$-subspace $L \leq W$ and $a \in K$ with $a^2 = 1$ such that every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $q$ for $A$ acts on $L$ by the scalar $a q$ and satisfies $\rho_M(\sigma)w - a w \in L$ for all $w \in W$.
--
--   This is the local–global compatibility of the $\lambda$-adic Galois representation attached to a weight-two newform, read directly inside the Tate module of $J_0(M)$: the Hecke eigenvalues give the Frobenius traces away from the level, and at a prime exactly dividing the level the restriction to a decomposition group has Steinberg shape (an unramified quadratic twist of a non-split extension with the Frobenius eigenvalues $a$ and $aq$ on the line $L$ and the quotient). It feeds the construction of the associated $\lambda$-adic representation with prescribed Frobenius characteristic polynomials at primes exactly dividing the level, used further downstream.
